# Tool rows over a native chat: each call shows what ran (a path, a pattern, a sub-agent's
# description with its own call under it, a host, a command with its description), and what the
# CLI said besides is a row (a subtask's end, a denial by settings, a notification). Then the
# command's row opened by the user's click: the whole command and what it printed. The stand-in
# `claude` replays chat-rows/fixtures.
{"env":{"OTTOSPACE_AGENTS_DIR":"{ROOT}/bin"}}
{"cmd":"split","kind":"empty"}
{"cmd":"task_new","line":"fix the login loop >app"}
{"cmd":"section","section":"tasks"}
{"click":"task:1","at":[0.3,0.3]}
{"click":"talk:talk-start"}
{"until":"drawer.native.chats.1.transcript.turn","is":null}
{"settle":1500}
{"shot":"rows"}
{"click":"chat-row:1:10"}
{"until":"drawer.native.chats.1.transcript.entries.10.expanded","is":true}
{"settle":500}
{"shot":"expanded"}
